   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] workshops",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Are you looking for a workshop on geometric morphometrics that teaches geomorph, or a workshop specifically focused on geomorph? The reason for asking is that geomorph is that the new version of the book that we wrote to accompany out textbook (A Practical Companion to Geometric Morphometrics for Biologists:  Running analyses in freely available software) is in the final stages of proofreading. This new version is devoted to running analyses in R, and it does focus on how to do them using geomorph. It does not explain much about the methods--we assume that you&#39;ve read about those and are now looking for guidance on how to apply them. When we teach workshops (or regular classes) we do not need to explain much about how to do the analyses beyond what&#39;s in the Practical Companion and the geomorph manual. We aren&#39;t teaching a workshop in the US in the near future (not until next summer) and the one that we&#39;re doing in March will be in Mexico. If you&#39;d like a copy of the revised Practical Companion, I can send you one once it&#39;s proofread/corrected.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Sep 21, 2018 at 10:42 AM, Adams, Dean [EEOBS] <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dca...@iastate.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
